    {
      "type": "reflect",
      "kicker": "Tell me what you know",
      "prompt": "When would you use a zone instead of an exact line?",
      "modelAnswer": "When price has reacted across a small area instead of one exact price. A zone captures where price actually showed behavior, so I don’t think a level “failed” just because price missed my line by a few points. But I keep the zone tight enough to describe the reaction, not a huge box that could mean anything."
